BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:legislature-senate-committee-on-business-and-commerce-20260729T0900@cal
 endars.changesaroundme.com
DTSTAMP:20260802T145154Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260729T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260729T110000
SUMMARY:Texas Senate - Business & Commerce: 765-kV lines and grid reliabili
 ty
LOCATION:Room E1.012 (Hearing Room)\, Texas Capitol Extension\, 1100 Congre
 ss Ave.\, Austin\, TX 78701
URL:https://capitol.texas.gov/tlodocs/89R/schedules/html/C5102026072909001.
 HTM
DESCRIPTION:Senate Committee on Business & Commerce\, chaired by Sen. Charl
 es\nSchwertner. Invited and public testimony on two interim charges:\n\nMa
 naging the Impacts of 765-kV Transmission Lines on Private Property\nRight
 s - reviewing the proposed route plans and their effect on homes\,\nbusine
 sses and communities\; whether current regulatory processes and\ntimelines
  adequately protect landowner rights\; and recommendations for\ntransmissi
 on planning\, permitting and siting.\n\nAssessing the State of the Texas E
 lectric Grid - SB 6 rulemaking\nincluding large load interconnection and t
 ransmission cost allocation\,\nERCOT load forecast confidence\, the Texas 
 Energy Fund and post-Uri\nreforms\, and whether the ERCOT market remains c
 ompetitive.\n\nPublic testimony is limited to 2 minutes per witness. Writt
 en testimony\nneeds 15 copies to the committee clerk plus a digital copy b
 y email.\nRegistration closes at 11am on the day of the hearing.\n\nNotice
  was marked REVISION - check the link for any later change.\n
CATEGORIES:hearing
X-CAM-ORG:legislature
END:VEVENT
